- @poland_event_queue: Publish the standard

@ind26_counter_coalition
title: Activate the standing democratic street coalition
subtitle: Three earlier counter-mobilisations have built a coalition that can protect its own route without draining every organisation for one emergency.
view-if: independence_counter_years >= 3 and independence_counter_coalition = 0
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Counter-mobilisation"; independence_counter_coalition = 1; independence_counter_years += 1; organiser_energy += 2; progressive_credibility += 7; minority_safety += 7; civic_patriotism += 3; public_trust += 3; far_right_street_capacity -= 4; far_right_agenda -= 2; braun_martyrdom -= 2; news_headline = "A standing democratic coalition out-organises the radical-right columns"

= Mobilisation becomes capacity

Anti-fascist groups, unions, neighbourhood organisations and minority networks
no longer rebuild their command structure each November. Shared stewards,
transport, medics and local assemblies put a larger democratic force beside the
people the nationalist columns once expected to isolate.

Because the coalition has its own route and public programme, Braun and Mentzen
cannot turn a hurried blockade into their organising story. The counter-march
protects threatened communities, keeps its organisers for the work after the
holiday and leaves the radical right facing a stronger street rather than a
larger emergency audience.

- @poland_event_queue: Carry the coalition beyond November

@ind26_divide
title: Amplify every split on the right
subtitle: Turn rival stages, insults and route disputes into a week-long leadership spectacle.
view-if: independence_counter_years < 3 or independence_counter_coalition = 1
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Exploit right fragmentation"; independence_counter_years += 1; media_capacity += 3; far_right_fragmentation += 5; far_right_street_capacity += 3; braun_martyrdom += 2; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "The Left wins a tactical media week and helps fill every radical-right column"

Lewica's media team clips every quarrel over speakers, symbols and precedence.
Kaczyński, Mentzen, Braun and Morawiecki each receive the humiliation of being
shown as one claimant among several—and the free publicity needed to summon a
larger column. We win the week's commentary while Warsaw inherits more
mobilised organisations than it had before our cameras arrived.

- @poland_event_queue: Start clipping

@constructive_motion_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — The constructive motion centres the named replacement, real defections and Lewica's coalition role rather than forecast-score manipulation.
title: A constructive no-confidence motion
subtitle: The opposition tests a constructive no-confidence motion
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-government-bench.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 30
order: 5
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 11 and government_party != "pis" and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and formation_in_progress = 0 and (government_coalition_dissent >= 45 or early_election_risk >= 45 or coalition_broken = 1)
on-arrival: {!
const pisSeats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.pis_seats) || 0);
const morawieckiCamp = Math.max(
    0,
    Number(Q.pis_morawiecki_camp) || 0
);
const sikorskiDemocraticSeats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.psl_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.centrum_seats) || 0);
const konfFamilySeats = Q.mentzen_bosak_split == 1
    ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.new_hope_seats) || 0) +
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.national_movement_seats) || 0)
    : Math.max(0, Number(Q.konf_seats) || 0);
Q.konf_family_seats = konfFamilySeats;
const sikorskiBlocSeats = sikorskiDemocraticSeats +
    konfFamilySeats;
const hostileDemocraticPartners = [
    [Q.ko_seats, Q.ko_relation],
    [Q.psl_seats, Q.psl_relation],
    [Q.p2050_seats, Q.p2050_relation],
    [Q.centrum_seats, Q.centrum_relation]
].filter(function(party) {
    return Number(party[0]) > 0 && Number(party[1]) <= 30;
}).length;
const sikorskiRoute =
    Q.government_party == "lewica" &&
    Q.left_in_government &&
    Q.ministry_ko_in_cabinet &&
    Q.president_name != "Radosław Sikorski" &&
    Q.prime_minister != "Radosław Sikorski" &&
    (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) >= 60 &&
    hostileDemocraticPartners >= 2 &&
    Q.coalition_viable_ko_konf &&
    (Number(Q.konf_normalisation) || 0) >= 40 &&
    Q.ko_konf_partner_line != "closed" &&
    Q.psl_konf_partner_line != "closed" &&
    konfFamilySeats > 0 &&
    sikorskiBlocSeats >= 231;
if (sikorskiRoute) {
    Q.constructive_candidate = "Radosław Sikorski";
    Q.constructive_base = sikorskiBlocSeats;
    Q.constructive_nomination_reason =
        "KO and the estranged democratic partners accept Konfederacja's votes to remove the Left-led cabinet.";
} else if (Q.pis_split || morawieckiCamp >= 25) {
    Q.constructive_candidate = "Mateusz Morawiecki";
    Q.constructive_base =
        pisSeats +
        (Q.pis_split ? morawieckiCamp : 0) +
        Math.round((Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0) * 0.15) +
        Math.round((Number(Q.psl_seats) || 0) * 0.10);
    Q.constructive_nomination_reason =
        "The Morawiecki camp claims it can recruit the centre.";
} else if ((Number(Q.far_right_agenda) || 0) >= 45) {
    Q.constructive_candidate = "Przemysław Czarnek";
    Q.constructive_base =
        pisSeats +
        Math.round(konfFamilySeats * 0.65);
    Q.constructive_nomination_reason =
        "PiS hardliners choose a culture-war route to 231.";
} else {
    Q.constructive_candidate = "Beata Szydło";
    Q.constructive_base =
        pisSeats +
        Math.round((Number(Q.psl_seats) || 0) * 0.25);
    Q.constructive_nomination_reason =
        "The opposition tries to recruit rural deputies with a welfare-nationalist offer.";
}
Q.news_headline =
    "The opposition files a constructive motion naming " +
    Q.constructive_candidate;
if (typeof polandCoalitionModel != "undefined") {
    Q.constructive_sitting_agreement_snapshot = {
        records: Array.isArray(Q.government_agreement_records)
            ? JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(Q.government_agreement_records)) : null,
        members: Array.isArray(Q.government_members)
            ? Q.government_members.slice() : null,
        supporters: Array.isArray(Q.government_supporters)
            ? Q.government_supporters.slice() : null,
        coalition_seats: Number(Q.coalition_seats) || 0,
        support_seats: Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 0,
        agreement_prime_minister: String(Q.government_agreement_prime_minister || "")
    };
    polandCoalitionModel.reconcile(Q);
    const proposedRoles = {
        lewica: "out", ko: "out", p2050: "out",
        psl: "out", pis: "out", konf: "out"
    };
    let sponsor = "pis";
    let candidateFamily = "pis";
    if (Q.constructive_candidate == "Radosław Sikorski") {
        sponsor = "ko";
        candidateFamily = "ko";
        proposedRoles.ko = "cabinet";
        proposedRoles.psl = "cabinet";
        proposedRoles.konf = "cabinet";
        proposedRoles.p2050 = "support";
        Q.constructive_sponsors = Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0));
    } else {
        proposedRoles.pis = "cabinet";
        proposedRoles.psl = "support";
        proposedRoles.p2050 = "support";
        if (Q.constructive_candidate == "Przemysław Czarnek") {
            proposedRoles.konf = "cabinet";
        }
        Q.constructive_sponsors = Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.pis_seats) || 0));
    }
    const agreementParties = polandCoalitionModel.parties(Q);
    polandCoalitionModel.initialise(Q, {
        mode: "constructive", candidate: Q.constructive_candidate,
        candidate_family: candidateFamily, sponsor: sponsor,
        seed_current: true, roles: proposedRoles,
        locked: agreementParties.map(function(party) { return party.id; }),
        allow_failed_vote: true,
        submit_scene: "constructive_roll_2026",
        submit_label: "Bring the named agreement to the roll call"
    });
    const firstAgreement = polandCoalitionModel.preview(Q);
    for (const party of firstAgreement.parties) {
        const decision = firstAgreement.decisions[party.id];
        if (decision.role != "out" && !decision.accepted) {
            Q.coalition_builder.roles[party.id] = "out";
        }
    }
}
!}

= November 2026 — Dismissal requires a replacement

At least 46 sponsors must name a candidate, and 231 deputies must vote for that
person. A failed motion does not dissolve the Sejm.

[? if constructive_candidate = "Radosław Sikorski": KO, the estranged
democratic coalition parties and Konfederacja have named <span class="party-ko"><b>Radosław Sikorski</b></span>.
The agreement gives the radical right cabinet offices in exchange for replacing
Lewica immediately.?][? if constructive_candidate != "Radosław Sikorski": The
opposition—not Lewica—has named **[+ constructive_candidate +]**.?]
[+ constructive_nomination_reason +] Its published starting count is **[+
constructive_base +]**. [? if constructive_candidate != "Radosław Sikorski":
Low PSL/Poland 2050 relations and coalition dissent can still add defections at
the roll call.?]

- @constructive_sikorski
