Several recruits retreat rather than defend the bargain; the nominee can no
longer present every prospective vote as ideological conversion.

{!<div class="coalition-builder-host" data-coalition-mode="constructive"></div>!}

- @constructive_roll_2026: Bring the named replacement to a roll call

@constructive_czarnek
title: Offer wavering partners a written coalition-repair protocol
subtitle: Give wavering partners a reason to repair this majority instead of creating another.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and constructive_candidate = "Przemysław Czarnek"
on-arrival: constructive_base -= 10; government_coalition_dissent -= 4; psl_relation += 2; p2050_relation += 2; ko_relation += 1; news_headline = "A written repair protocol closes several routes to the opposition nominee"

We put coalition repairs into writing before the opposition can price the same
deputies. PSL and Poland 2050 keep their leverage, but fewer MPs need a PiS
replacement cabinet to exercise it.

{!<div class="coalition-builder-host" data-coalition-mode="constructive"></div>!}

- @constructive_roll_2026: Bring the named replacement to a roll call

@constructive_szydlo
title: Permit a free Lewica vote and expose the real defectors
subtitle: Refuse a central whip and make every Lewica defection personal and visible.
view-if: constructive_candidate = "Beata Szydło"
on-arrival: {!
Q.constructive_left_defections = Math.min(
    Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.left_seats) || 0)),
    Math.max(
        0,
        Math.round((Number(Q.left_seats) || 0) * 0.08)
    )
);
Q.constructive_base += Q.constructive_left_defections;
Q.party_unity -= 5;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica refuses a central whip and makes every defection visible";
!}

We lift the whip and force each MP to own the named replacement. A small group
crosses; the public gets an honest roll call and the party inherits a breach
that will not disappear when the motion ends.

{!<div class="coalition-builder-host" data-coalition-mode="constructive"></div>!}

- @constructive_roll_2026: Bring the named replacement to a roll call

@constructive_defend_2026
title: Run a full coalition whip against the named nominee
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Turn fear of the named replacement into governing unity.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The whip operation lacks capacity.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; constructive_base -= 18; government_coalition_dissent -= 6; party_unity += 2; ko_relation += 2; psl_relation += 2; p2050_relation += 2; news_headline = "The governing clubs turn the named replacement vote into defensive unity"

Our whips make every dispute answer one question: whether it is worth installing
**[+ constructive_candidate +]** today. The coalition rediscovers unity, even
if none of its older disagreements has been solved.

{!<div class="coalition-builder-host" data-coalition-mode="constructive"></div>!}

- @constructive_roll_2026: Bring the named replacement to a roll call

@constructive_roll_2026
title: Constructive roll call
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const proposedAgreement = typeof polandCoalitionModel != "undefined" &&
    Q.coalition_builder && Q.coalition_builder.context.mode == "constructive"
        ? polandCoalitionModel.preview(Q) : null;
Q.constructive_relation_recruits = 0;
Q.constructive_coalition_defections = 0;
Q.constructive_roll_variance = 0;
Q.constructive_yes = proposedAgreement
    ? proposedAgreement.effective_seats
    : Math.max(0, Math.min(460, Math.round(Number(Q.constructive_base) || 0)));
Q.constructive_passed =
    (Number(Q.constructive_sponsors) || 0) >= 46 &&
    (proposedAgreement ? proposedAgreement.ok : Q.constructive_yes >= 231)
        ? 1 : 0;
Q.confidence_yes = Q.constructive_yes;
Q.confidence_abstain = 0;
Q.confidence_no = Math.max(
    0,
    460 - Q.confidence_yes - Q.confidence_abstain
);
Q.confidence_candidate = Q.constructive_candidate;
Q.confidence_mode = "Constructive no confidence";
Q.confidence_present = 460;
Q.confidence_threshold = 231;
if (Q.constructive_passed) {
    const sikorskiReplacement =
        Q.constructive_candidate == "Radosław Sikorski";
    if (proposedAgreement) polandCoalitionModel.commit(Q);
    Q.government_removed_by_vonc = 1;
    Q.prime_minister = Q.constructive_candidate;
    Q.prime_minister_intro_return = sikorskiReplacement
        ? "sikorski_compact_2026"
        : "event_queue";
    Q.prime_minister_intro_pending = 1;
    Q.government_name = Q.constructive_candidate + " replacement cabinet";
    Q.government_party = sikorskiReplacement ? "ko" : "pis";
    Q.government_owner = sikorskiReplacement
        ? "Sikorski's KO–centre–Konfederacja compact"
        : "PiS and its governing partners";
    Q.left_in_government = 0;
    Q.left_cabinet_committed = 0;
    Q.left_cabinet_model = "Opposition";
    Q.ministries_finalized = 1;
    Q.ministry_allocation_mode = "settled";
    Q.ministry_return_mode = "event_queue";
    Q.budget = 0;
    Q.budget_authority =
        "Opposition — no state spending authority";
    Q.position = "Parliamentary opposition";
    Q.coalition_status = sikorskiReplacement
        ? "KO–centre–Konfederacja constructive majority"
        : "Constructive replacement majority";
    if (!proposedAgreement) {
        Q.coalition_seats = sikorskiReplacement
            ? Math.min(
                Number(Q.sejm_total) || 460,
                Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0) +
                Math.max(0, Number(Q.psl_seats) || 0) +
                Math.max(0, Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0) +
                (Q.mentzen_bosak_split == 1
                    ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.new_hope_seats) || 0) +
                        Math.max(0, Number(Q.national_movement_seats) || 0)
                    : Math.max(0, Number(Q.konf_seats) || 0))
            )
            : Math.max(0, Number(Q.pis_seats) || 0);
    }
    Q.government_support_seats = Q.constructive_yes;
    Q.government_has_confidence = 1;
    Q.caretaker_government = 0;
    Q.formation_in_progress = 0;
    Q.formation_complete = 1;
    Q.coalition_broken = 0;
    Q.snap_election_requested = 0;
    // Losing the cabinet to PiS is a KO failure its regions have to be told
    // about; it feeds the collapse meter in poland_ko_collapse.
    if (!sikorskiReplacement) {
        Q.ko_collapse_shock = (Number(Q.ko_collapse_shock) || 0) + 18;
    }
    if ((Number(Q.constructive_left_defections) || 0) > 0) {
        const durableLeftDefections = Math.min(
            Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.left_seats) || 0)),
            Math.max(
                0,
                Math.round(
                    Number(Q.constructive_left_defections) || 0
                )
            )
        );
        Q.left_seats = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q.left_seats) || 0) - durableLeftDefections
        );
        Q.left_committed_seats = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q.left_committed_seats) || 0) -
                durableLeftDefections
        );
        Q.left_family_seats = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q.left_family_seats) || 0) -
                durableLeftDefections
        );
        Q.coalition_democratic_seats = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q.coalition_democratic_seats) || 0) -
                durableLeftDefections
        );
        Q.other_seats =
            Math.max(0, Number(Q.other_seats) || 0) +
            durableLeftDefections;
    }
    const inReplacementCabinet = function(id) {
        const decision = proposedAgreement && proposedAgreement.decisions[id];
        return decision && decision.accepted && decision.role == "cabinet";
    };
    const p2050InCabinet = inReplacementCabinet("p2050");
    const pslInCabinet = inReplacementCabinet("psl");
    const konfInCabinet = inReplacementCabinet("konf");
    const replacementCabinet = sikorskiReplacement ? {
        labor: ["KO", "Marzena Okła-Drewnowicz"],
        equality: ["KO", "Monika Rosa"],
        housing: ["KO", "Krystyna Sibińska"],
        health: ["KO", "Izabela Leszczyna"],
        digital: p2050InCabinet
            ? ["Poland 2050", "Michał Gramatyka"]
            : ["KO", "Jan Grabiec"],
        science: ["KO", "Barbara Nowacka"],
        interior: ["KO", "Marcin Kierwiński"],
        finance: ["Konfederacja", "Sławomir Mentzen"],
        economy: ["Konfederacja", "Przemysław Wipler"],
        justice: ["KO", "Adam Bodnar"],
        foreign: ["KO", "Paweł Kowal"],
        agriculture: pslInCabinet
            ? ["PSL", "Czesław Siekierski"]
            : ["KO", "Dorota Niedziela"],
        defence: pslInCabinet
            ? ["PSL", "Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz"]
            : ["KO", "Tomasz Siemoniak"]
    } : {
        labor: ["PiS", "Dorota Bojemska"],
        equality: ["PiS", "Anna Schmidt"],
        housing: ["PiS", "Piotr Uściński"],
        health: ["PiS", "Ewa Krajewska"],
        digital: ["PiS", "Janusz Cieszyński"],
        science: ["PiS", "Krzysztof Szczucki"],
        interior: ["PiS", "Paweł Szefernaker"],
        finance: konfInCabinet
            ? ["Konfederacja", "Sławomir Mentzen"]
            : ["PiS", "Andrzej Kosztowniak"],
        economy: konfInCabinet
            ? ["Konfederacja", "Przemysław Wipler"]
            : ["PiS", "Marlena Maląg"],
        justice: ["PiS", "Marcin Warchoł"],
        foreign: ["PiS", "Szymon Szynkowski vel Sęk"],
        agriculture: ["PiS", "Anna Gembicka"],
        defence: ["PiS", "Mariusz Błaszczak"]
    };
    for (const portfolio of Object.keys(replacementCabinet)) {
        Q[portfolio + "_minister_party"] =
            replacementCabinet[portfolio][0];
        Q[portfolio + "_minister"] =
            replacementCabinet[portfolio][1];
    }
    Q.family_minister_party = Q.labor_minister_party;
    Q.family_minister = Q.labor_minister;
    Q.ministry_count = 0;
    Q.ministry_ko_in_cabinet = sikorskiReplacement ? 1 : 0;
    Q.ministry_pis_in_cabinet = sikorskiReplacement ? 0 : 1;
    Q.ministry_p2050_in_cabinet = p2050InCabinet ? 1 : 0;
    Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet = pslInCabinet ? 1 : 0;
    Q.ministry_konf_in_cabinet = konfInCabinet ? 1 : 0;
    Q.sikorski_konf_cabinet = sikorskiReplacement ? 1 : 0;
    Q.sikorski_nightmare = sikorskiReplacement ? 1 : 0;
    Q.cabinet_roster_government_party = sikorskiReplacement ? "ko" : "pis";
    Q.news_headline = sikorskiReplacement
        ? "Sikorski replaces the Left with Konfederacja's decisive votes"
        : Q.constructive_candidate + " replaces the prime minister";
    Q.constructive_sitting_agreement_snapshot = null;
} else {
    const sitting = Q.constructive_sitting_agreement_snapshot;
    if (sitting) {
        Q.government_agreement_records = sitting.records;
        Q.government_members = sitting.members;
        Q.government_supporters = sitting.supporters;
        Q.coalition_seats = sitting.coalition_seats;
        Q.government_support_seats = sitting.support_seats;
        Q.government_agreement_prime_minister = sitting.agreement_prime_minister;
    }
    Q.coalition_builder = null;
    Q.constructive_sitting_agreement_snapshot = null;
    Q.news_headline =
        "The constructive motion fails with " +
        Q.constructive_yes + " votes";
}
!}

= Constructive vote

**[+ constructive_candidate +]: [+ constructive_yes +] yes**

The nominee needed **46 named sponsors** and a signed agreement pledging 231
votes. Every displayed party decision is deterministic: accepted clubs pledge
their recorded seats, refused invitations supply none, and no anonymous
last-minute variance is added.

[? if constructive_passed: **[+ constructive_candidate +]** takes office
immediately with the MPs who signed the replacement. Lewica loses its ministries
and any of our defectors leave a permanent hole in the democratic majority; no
separate destructive vote or automatic election follows.?]
[? if not constructive_passed: The cabinet survives until the budget. Its
partners have seen exactly who was willing to leave, while PiS has learned that
this named alternative could not reach 231.?]

